{
 "id": "2026-11-27-a",
 "title": "Where do your returns actually go? 📦",
 "description": "Americans sent back about $850 billion of merchandise in 2025 (NRF), roughly 16% of everything bought. Each return has to be shipped back, inspected, cleaned and repacked, which often costs more than the item is worth. Opened items rarely go back on the shelf as new; many are sold in bulk to liquidators and resellers, and experts estimate about a quarter are thrown away, nearly 6 billion pounds of landfill a year (Optoro estimate). Retailers say 9% of returns are fraudulent. The receipt costs in the video are illustrative.\n\nSources: National Retail Federation & Happy Returns, 2025 Retail Returns Landscape; NPR; Mental Floss.",
